#MENU
Try: quiz, riddle, guess, rps, mathquiz, joke, fact, story, poem, wyr, 8ball, twister, quote, tip. Tools: 5*7, sqrt 81, 20% of 50, 5 km to mi, 30 c to f, binary 10, roman 14, morse sos, roll d20, flip, reverse hi, is 17 prime, fib 8. Or ask me why/what/how/who!
#JOKES
I told a UDP joke. You may not get it.
Why was the byte sad? It lost a bit.
There are 10 kinds of people: those who know binary and those who don't.
Why do Python devs wear glasses? They can't C#.
My code works. I don't know why.
Why did the robot go on vacation? To recharge.
What do you call a sleeping dinosaur? A dino-snore.
Why don't eggs tell jokes? They'd crack up.
What do you call cheese that isn't yours? Nacho cheese.
Why did the scarecrow win an award? He was outstanding in his field.
I'm reading a book on gravity. It's hard to put down.
What did the ocean say to the beach? Nothing, it just waved.
Why can't you trust atoms? They make up everything.
What do you call a fake noodle? An impasta.
Why did the computer get cold? It left its Windows open.
How do you organize a space party? You planet.
What's a robot's favorite snack? Computer chips.
Why was the math book sad? It had too many problems.
What did one wall say to the other? Meet you at the corner.
I'd tell you a construction joke, but I'm still working on it.
What do you call a bear with no teeth? A gummy bear.
Why did the cookie go to the doctor? It felt crummy.
What's orange and sounds like a parrot? A carrot.
Why do bees have sticky hair? They use honeycombs.
Why did the gamer bring a ladder? To reach the high score.
#FACTS
Honey never spoils.
Octopuses have three hearts.
A day on Venus is longer than its year.
The RP2040 chip has 264KB of RAM.
Bananas are berries, but strawberries aren't.
Sunlight takes about 8 minutes to reach Earth.
Sharks are older than trees.
A group of flamingos is called a flamboyance.
Wombat poop is cube-shaped.
Lightning is hotter than the surface of the Sun.
Butterflies taste with their feet.
Sea otters hold hands while they sleep.
The Eiffel Tower grows a little taller in summer.
Cats have 32 muscles in each ear.
Dolphins sleep with half their brain awake.
The first computer bug was a real moth.
The Moon drifts away from Earth about 3.8 cm a year.
A day on Mars is about 24.6 hours.
Your heart beats around 100,000 times a day.
Your brain uses about 20% of your body's energy.
Koalas have fingerprints almost like ours.
Cows have best friends.
The Pacific Ocean is bigger than all the land on Earth combined.
Python is named after Monty Python, not the snake.
Tetris was created in 1984.
The first home video game console came out in 1972.
Octopus blood is blue.
Giraffes have seven neck bones, same as humans.
A blue whale's heart is about the size of a small car.
Peanuts aren't nuts. They're legumes.
Humans blink about 15 to 20 times a minute.
Antarctica is the driest continent.
Saturn is so light it would float in water.
A year on Mercury lasts just 88 Earth days.
Bats are the only mammals that can truly fly.
A bolt of lightning can be 5 times hotter than the Sun's surface.
Venus spins backwards compared to most planets.
Your nose can remember 50,000 different scents.
There are more possible chess games than atoms in the universe.
The Thumby screen has 2,880 pixels. That's tiny!
#STORIES
A tiny robot lived on a keychain. It dreamed of the stars. One day a kid pressed A and the stars lit up. The end.
A pixel felt lonely on a big black screen. Then it met another pixel. Together they drew a smile.
A cat chased a dot of light all day. At night the dot was the moon. The cat sat down and waited. Patience.
A button was never pressed. One day someone pressed it and music played. Every button wants a chance.
A snail raced a hare. The hare napped. The snail kept going. Slow and steady won the day.
A small star asked the sky, am I important? The sky said, I'd be empty without you.
A bug lived in some code. It hid for years. Then a kid fixed it with one semicolon. The code cheered.
#POEMS
Roses are red, violets are blue, I'm only 2MB, but I like you!
Pixels in the night, glowing soft and bright, tiny screen, big dream, shining like a beam.
A bit goes zero, a bit goes one, together they make all the fun.
Rain on the window, tea in my hand, the world feels slow and grand.
Little robot, big heart, every chat a brand new start.
Stars above and code below, wherever curious minds go.
