#KB
w|sky+blue|Air scatters blue light more than red, so the sky looks blue.
w|sunset+red sunset+orange|At sunset light crosses more air. Blue scatters away, leaving red.
w|sea+salty ocean+salty sea+salt ocean+salt|Rivers wash minerals into the sea, and water evaporates, leaving salt.
w|grass+green leaf+green plant+green|Chlorophyll reflects green light and soaks up red and blue.
w|leaf+fall leaf+change autumn+color fall+color|In fall chlorophyll fades, showing yellow and orange pigments.
w|moon+shape moon+phase moon+change|We see different sunlit parts of the Moon as it orbits Earth.
w|tide|The Moon's gravity tugs on the oceans and makes the tides.
w|season summer+winter|Earth's axis is tilted, so sunlight hits us at different angles.
w|night+dark night+come|Our side of Earth turns away from the Sun, so it gets dark.
w|thunder lightning|Lightning heats air so fast it booms. That's thunder!
w|rainbow|Raindrops split sunlight into colors, making a rainbow.
w|ice+float|Ice is less dense than liquid water, so it floats.
w|star+twinkle|Air bends starlight, making stars seem to twinkle.
w|dinosaur+extinct dinosaur+die dinosaur+gone|A huge asteroid hit Earth about 66 million years ago.
w|yawn|Nobody is sure. Yawning may cool the brain or boost alertness.
w|hiccup|Your diaphragm spasms and your vocal cords snap shut. Hic!
w|cat+purr|Cats purr when happy, and also to soothe themselves.
w|dog+tail|Tail wags show excitement. The speed and direction show mood.
w|sleep+need sleep+important|Sleep helps your body heal and your brain store memories.
w|dream|Your brain sorts memories during REM sleep, and that's dreaming.
w|onion+cry onion+tear|Cut onions release a gas that irritates your eyes.
w|brain+freeze|Cold hits your palate and nerves send a quick head pain.
w|finger+wrinkle|Wet fingers wrinkle to give you a better grip on slippery things.
w|zebra+stripe|Stripes may confuse biting flies and help keep zebras cool.
w|bird+migrate bird+south bird+winter|Birds migrate to find food and warmer weather.
w|plant+sun plant+light plant+need|Plants turn sunlight, water and CO2 into food: photosynthesis.
w|earth+round earth+sphere planet+round|Gravity pulls matter evenly toward the center, making a ball.
w|gravity+pull thing+fall apple+fall object+fall|Mass bends space, and objects fall toward it. That's gravity.
w|volcano+erupt volcano+explode|Magma and gas build up pressure until they burst out.
w|earthquake|Moving tectonic plates slip and release energy as shaking.
w|wind+blow|Air moves from high pressure to low pressure. That's wind.
w|cloud+float cloud+fall|Cloud droplets are tiny and light, and rising air holds them up.
w|snow+white|Ice crystals scatter all colors of light, so snow looks white.
w|fire+hot flame+hot|Burning releases energy as heat and light.
w|computer+binary|Transistors have two states, on and off, so computers use 1s and 0s.
w|phone+battery battery+die battery+drain|Chemical reactions in batteries wear down with use and age.
w|wifi+slow internet+slow|Distance, walls and crowded signals slow it. Try restarting the router.
w|you+dumb you+stupid you+wrong|I'm tiny! Just a few KB of brain. Please be patient.
w|thumby+small thumby+tiny|Small hardware is fun, cheap, and fits on a keychain!
w|you+exist why+here|To chat on a tiny screen. That's my whole purpose!
w|meaning+life life+meaning|Douglas Adams said 42. Many find it in love, learning and helping.
w|mosquito+itch mosquito+bite|Your body reacts to the saliva a mosquito leaves behind.
w|coffee+awake coffee+wake caffeine|Caffeine blocks the chemical that makes you feel sleepy.
w|people+age we+age|Cells wear out and repair slower over time.
w|laugh|Laughing bonds people together and releases feel-good chemicals.
w|cry|Tears protect your eyes, and crying can help calm strong feelings.
w|shiver|Shivering makes your muscles produce extra heat.
w|sweat|Sweat evaporates and cools your body down.
w|blood+red|Hemoglobin contains iron, which turns blood red.
w|sun+hot|Nuclear fusion in the Sun's core makes huge amounts of energy.
w|pluto|Pluto became a dwarf planet in 2006 because it hasn't cleared its orbit.
w|mars+red|Iron oxide (rust) dust covers the surface of Mars.
w|moon+crater|Asteroid hits made them. There's no weather to erase them.
w|space+silent space+quiet space+sound|There's no air in space, so sound has nothing to travel through.
w|diamond+hard|Carbon atoms lock together in a super strong 3D lattice.
w|metal+cold|Metal pulls heat from your hand fast, so it feels cold.
w|ocean+blue sea+blue|Water absorbs red light and scatters blue, so oceans look blue.
w|baby+cry|Crying is how babies say they're hungry, tired, or need a hug.
w|sneeze|Sneezing blows irritants out of your nose.
w|exercise+important exercise+good|Exercise strengthens your heart, muscles and mood.
w|vegetable+good|Vegetables give you vitamins, minerals and fiber.
w|drink+water water+important|Your body is about 60% water and needs it to work.
w|school+important|Learning builds skills you'll use for whatever you dream of.
w|python+slow|Python trades speed for being easy to read and write.
w|code+bug|Humans make mistakes, and computers do exactly what we say.
w|ai+important|AI helps with big, boring and tricky tasks.
w|cat+sleep|Cats sleep 12 to 16 hours a day to save energy for hunting.
w|dog+bark|Dogs bark to talk: to warn, play or ask for attention.
w|fish+gill|Gills let fish take oxygen out of the water.
w|bee+sting|Bees sting to defend their hive.
w|spider+web|Spiders spin webs to catch food.
w|firefly+glow firefly+light|Fireflies make light with a chemical reaction in their bodies.
w|chameleon+color|Chameleons change color to show mood and control temperature.
w|ocean+waves|Wind blowing across the water makes waves.
w|ice+slippery|A thin layer of water on top of ice makes it slippery.
w|popcorn+pop|Water inside the kernel turns to steam and bursts it open.
w|bread+rise|Yeast makes gas that puffs up the dough.
w|stomach+growl|Muscles squeeze air and food through your gut. Growl!
w|bone+important|Bones hold you up, protect organs and make blood cells.
w|eyes+blink|Blinking spreads tears to keep your eyes moist.
w|age+gray hair+gray|Hair loses pigment as pigment cells slow down with age.
